<title>CANADA: Starbucks staff in Vancouver approve strike.</title>
<headline>Starbucks staff in Vancouver approve strike.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unionized workers at nine Starbucks Corp locations in Vancouver have voted 92 percent in favor of a strike, the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The vote means the workers could go on strike at any time within the next three months after giving 72 hours notice.</p>
<p>The company and officials of the Canadian Auto Workers union will meet with a mediator from the Labor Relations Board next week to continue contract negotiations.</p>
<p>The eight company outlets and a distribution center employ 110 union workers.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
</text>
